  "summary": "A speed reducer (gearbox) lowers speed and raises torque between a motor and a slow machine. In this two-stage helical reducer, a 16-tooth pinion drives a 32-tooth gear (2:1), and a 15-tooth pinion on the same intermediate shaft drives a 45-tooth gear (3:1) — 6:1 overall. Helical teeth run quietly and carry high loads; the gears dip into an oil bath for lubrication.",
  "classification": {
    "family": "Gear drive",
    "type": "Parallel-shaft helical reducer, two stages"
  },
